{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ouhwkqcef2lnwr7hzngtswqmdefqsgqn3nyglfxerrtsccyygvda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, independently confirmed.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit (`lib.c`, 90 lines) exporting exactly one symbol: `char *searchAndReplace(const char *orig, const char *search, const char *value)`. No `#ifdef`s, no cmake options, and `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section** — so the only feature combinations are `<default>` and `--no-default-features` (both verified, in **release *and* debug** profiles).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (created in the crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — source inventory + `nm -D` diff. C exports `searchAndReplace`; Rust exports `searchAndReplace`; diff is **empty**, 0 unresolved non-libc imports.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 12 rows, mechanically derived: the no-match `strdup` early return, all 5 `return NULL` allocation-failure sites (strdup / prefix malloc / value realloc / gap realloc / tail realloc), the 3 unchecked-NULL derefs, the two empty-`search` non-termination variants, and an explicit \"no enum parameters exist\" row.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 27 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (match at 0 / >0, 1 vs many matches, adjacent vs gap, tail vs no tail, `value` empty/shorter/equal/longer, overlapping occurrences, high/non-UTF8 bytes, long inputs, aliasing).\n- **`VERIFICATION.md`** — the completion gate with evidence.\n\n## Phases B–D results\n\nAll tests load **both** `.so`s with `libloading` and call only exported symbols. **46 tests pass**: 28 differential (**78 016 randomized cases = 156 033 FFI calls**, fixed seeds), 16 error-path, 2 symbol-parity. Allocation failures are forced deterministically via `fork()` + `RLIMIT_AS`; faults/hangs are compared by child wait status.\n\nTwo real bugs were found and fixed (never in the C):\n\n1. **`src/lib.rs` diverged on NULL arguments in debug builds** — the hand-rolled `strlen` hit rustc's null-deref instrumentation and aborted (`SIGABRT`) where C faults (`SIGSEGV`). The translation now calls the same libc primitives the C calls (`strlen`/`strstr`/`strncpy`/`strdup`), making glibc's empty-needle `strstr`, `strncpy`'s zero-padding, and the NULL fault identical by construction in every profile. The Rust `.so` now imports exactly the same six libc symbols as the C `.so`.\n2. **Two test-infrastructure defects** that were silently hiding rows: `RLIMIT_AS` couldn't fail a 24 MiB allocation (glibc serves ≤32 MiB from a thread arena's pre-reserved region — raised to 128 MiB), and one boundary test accidentally generated the empty-`search` non-terminating path in-process, leaking until the test binary aborted.\n\nI also mutation-tested the harness: breaking the prefix condition failed 17/28 Phase B tests with byte-level divergence reports, and deleting a `realloc` NULL check failed Phase C `err04`/`err11` (`C=NULL` vs `Rust=SIGSEGV`) — so the suite genuinely detects divergence. `run_verification.sh` reproduces the whole sweep and reports `ALL CHECKS PASSED`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the instructed `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_read_input_tokens":184593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":268,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bc34e8f-fde7-4761-8d52-c1baa11cda45","uuid":"13a30b4e-7dd6-46c1-ae24-62508dee3bc6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:08:32.864Z"}
